The faces in `fonts/` are Adwaita Sans and Adwaita Mono, the interface fonts
GNOME and Fedora ship, cut down to the characters the shell draws. Both are
licensed under the SIL Open Font License, version 1.1, which the subsets carry
with them.

    Copyright 2023 The Adwaita Fonts Project Authors
    https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/adwaita-fonts

The license text is at https://openfontlicense.org. In short: the font and
anything derived from it may be used, studied, modified and redistributed
freely, it may be bundled with software under any license, and it may not be
sold on its own.

`scripts/subset-font.py` makes the subsets from the full faces, keeping the
ninety five characters the shell draws. The build does not run it, so a machine
without the originals still builds the tree. `build/initrd.tar` carries the
result, and `modules/desktop/truetype.cpp` parses and rasterises it at run
time: no glyph is ever compiled into a source file.
